WEBVTT

NOTE English visual guide. Editorial descriptions of on-screen concepts; no spoken narration.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.800
Training adjusts the Transformer to predict the next character from preceding context.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.200
Targets are the input stream shifted by one character. A batch of 32 windows with 64 positions

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.400
provides 2,048 target predictions.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.800
Teacher forcing supplies known previous tokens during training. A causal mask allows all positions

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:33.600
to be trained in parallel without revealing their future answers.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.200
Cross-entropy is minus the natural logarithm of the probability assigned to the correct next token.

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:44.400
Average it over the prediction positions.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:50.800
Judge loss against baselines. In this reference run, uniform guessing scores 4.174; frequency-based

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.600
and previous-letter baselines are stronger comparisons.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.800
The training toolkit includes AdamW, learning-rate warmup, cosine decay and gradient clipping.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.200
Warmup increases the learning rate initially; decay reduces it later. Clipping limits a gradient

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:18.400
norm when it exceeds the selected threshold.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.400
Short learning-rate trials compare validation loss. The chosen 0.01 is specific to this small model

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.800
and experiment.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.400
The main reference run improves validation loss to about 1.742 in 1,400 steps. Perplexity exp(1.742)

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:40.800
is approximately 5.7, not an accuracy percentage.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:48.000
Compare selected predictions before and after training to see how context can improve the

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.000
probability of a plausible next character.

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.000
Changing the available context length tests how much the trained model benefits from preceding

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:01.000
characters.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:09.400
Average attention weights visualize where this model mixes information, but do not by themselves

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.800
establish causal explanations.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:22.400
Pause: is a validation loss of 2.5 impressive if the previous-letter baseline already scores 2.482?

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:26.800
Why can training evaluate 64 positions together?

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.800
A loss of 2.5 does not beat that baseline. Known targets plus causal masking make parallel

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:37.600
teacher-forced training possible.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.600
Recap training and evaluation. Continue to section 8 of this lesson to see how generation differs:

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:51.200
predict a token, append it, and repeat.
